    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "buffer.rs has one test module named tests.  Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Do not add a second module with the same name. Add char_at on TextBuffer. Use one if. Do not nest an if inside it. if at.0 >= self.len().0 { return None; } Then return Some(self.text.char(at.0)). Do not touch len, line_count, line_col, offset, slice, or apply. The test char_at_is_none_past_the_end uses TextBuffer::from_str of ab. Offset 0 returns Some a. Offset 1 returns Some b. Offset 2 returns None. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
